IMPORT prelude

-- Motor Accidents (Lifetime Care and Support) Act 2006 (NSW) -- s 54 (recovery of lifetime care and support payments),
-- from the seat of the person the Authority may recover from: the owner or driver of an uninsured vehicle, or another
-- person partly at fault.
--
-- SEAT: the owner or driver of the motor vehicle whose fault caused a participant's motor accident injury, or another
-- person (not the owner or driver of a motor vehicle) whose fault partly caused it. The questions are theirs: "Can the
-- Authority recover the participant's care costs from me?" and "How much?". The participant's own seat is in
-- ltcs-scheme.l4; the two modules share no names and neither imports the other (the participant's questions do not
-- turn on s 54). The Authority and the court get no seat.
--
-- ANSWERS. JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's words say no (an "if" or "only if" condition, "is not entitled", "does
-- not permit", the "appropriate person ... is" definition, a defence proved, read as "this section gives no recovery
-- from you on these facts"); NOTHING with a "NOTHING-kind" comment where the Act does not answer.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 1 July 2021; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Accidents (Lifetime Care and Support) Act 2006 -- s 54, the owner's or driver's seat`

-- s 54(5) "The appropriate person from whom the Authority may recover is (a) unless paragraph (b) applies -- the person
-- who at the time of the motor accident was the owner of the motor vehicle or, if at that time some other person was
-- driving the motor vehicle, the owner and the driver jointly or either of them severally"; s 54(3) "a person (other
-- than the owner or driver of a motor vehicle)" partly at fault.
DECLARE `My part in the accident` IS ONE OF
    `I owned the vehicle and was driving it`
    `I owned the vehicle and someone else was driving it`
    `I was driving the vehicle and someone else owned it`
    `I was partly at fault but was not the owner or driver of a motor vehicle`
    `none of these`

-- s 54(1) "The Authority is entitled to recover from the appropriate person as a debt due to the Authority the present
-- value of its treatment and care liabilities ... if (a) the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver of a
-- motor vehicle in the use or operation of the vehicle, and (b) at the time of the motor accident there was no
-- third-party policy in force in relation to the motor vehicle concerned." s 54(5)(b): where the vehicle was covered by
-- an interstate or Commonwealth compulsory scheme, the insurer or the person liable under it is the appropriate person,
-- not the owner or driver. s 54(6) "only if the injury is an injury to which Chapter 3 of the Motor Accidents
-- Compensation Act 1999 applies". s 54(7) the owner's defence: someone else was driving without the owner's authority.
-- s 54(8) the driver's defence: driving with the owner's authority (or reasonably believing so) and reasonably believing
-- a third-party policy was in force. s 54(9) "not entitled to recover" from the owner or driver of a vehicle that was
-- not required to be registered, was exempt, or was not required to be insured. s 54(11) "does not permit" recovery if
-- the participant bought in under s 7A(1). s 54(3) is read as standing apart from s 54(1)'s uninsured-vehicle conditions
-- (fork F9); s 54(6) and (11) govern it too, as they speak of recovery "under this section".
GIVEN `my part` IS A `My part in the accident`, `the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver` IS A BOOLEAN, `no third-party policy was in force for the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN, `the vehicle was covered by an interstate or Commonwealth compulsory scheme` IS A BOOLEAN, `Chapter 3 of the 1999 Act applies to the injury` IS A BOOLEAN, `the vehicle did not have to be registered or insured` IS A BOOLEAN, `the participant bought in under section 7A` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court is satisfied someone drove without my authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court is satisfied of the driver's defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Authority may recover under s 54 from` `my part` `fault` `the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver` `uninsured` `no third-party policy was in force for the vehicle` `interstate` `the vehicle was covered by an interstate or Commonwealth compulsory scheme` `chapter 3` `Chapter 3 of the 1999 Act applies to the injury` `exempt` `the vehicle did not have to be registered or insured` `bought in` `the participant bought in under section 7A` `owner's defence` `the court is satisfied someone drove without my authority` `driver's defence` `the court is satisfied of the driver's defence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `my part` EQUALS `none of these` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `Chapter 3 of the 1999 Act applies to the injury`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the participant bought in under section 7A` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `my part` EQUALS `I was partly at fault but was not the owner or driver of a motor vehicle` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF (NOT `the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `no third-party policy was in force for the vehicle`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the vehicle was covered by an interstate or Commonwealth compulsory scheme` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the vehicle did not have to be registered or insured` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `my part` EQUALS `I owned the vehicle and someone else was driving it` AND `the court is satisfied someone drove without my authority` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `my part` EQUALS `I was driving the vehicle and someone else owned it` AND `the court is satisfied of the driver's defence` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@export Can the Lifetime Care and Support Authority recover from me what it pays for an injured participant's treatment and care (s 54)?
GIVEN `my part in the accident` IS A `My part in the accident` @desc Your part in the accident. One of: "I owned the vehicle and was driving it", "I owned the vehicle and someone else was driving it", "I was driving the vehicle and someone else owned it", "I was partly at fault but was not the owner or driver of a motor vehicle", "none of these"
      `the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the participant's injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver of the vehicle in its use or operation
      `no third-party policy was in force for the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the accident, there was no NSW compulsory third-party policy in force for the vehicle
      `the vehicle was covered by an interstate or Commonwealth compulsory scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was covered by compulsory third-party personal injury insurance, or a compulsory motor accident compensation scheme, under the law of a place other than New South Wales or of the Commonwealth
      `Chapter 3 of the 1999 Act applies to the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is one to which Chapter 3 of the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999 applies (under section 3B of that Act)
      `the vehicle did not have to be registered or insured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was, at the time, not required to be registered, exempt from registration, or (if it had to be registered) not required to be insured under the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999
      `the participant bought in under section 7A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured participant paid the Authority a contribution to buy into the Scheme under section 7A for these injuries
      `the court is satisfied someone drove without my authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are the owner and someone else was driving: whether you establish to the court's satisfaction that the driver was driving without your authority
      `the court is satisfied of the driver's defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were the driver and someone else owned the vehicle: whether you establish to the court's satisfaction that you drove with the owner's authority (or reasonably believed, and did believe, you had it) and that you reasonably believed, and did believe, a third-party policy was in force
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` MEANS
    `the Authority may recover under s 54 from` `my part in the accident` `fault` `the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver` `uninsured` `no third-party policy was in force for the vehicle` `interstate` `the vehicle was covered by an interstate or Commonwealth compulsory scheme` `chapter 3` `Chapter 3 of the 1999 Act applies to the injury` `exempt` `the vehicle did not have to be registered or insured` `bought in` `the participant bought in under section 7A` `owner's defence` `the court is satisfied someone drove without my authority` `driver's defence` `the court is satisfied of the driver's defence`

-- s 54(4) the present value of the treatment and care liabilities is "(a) amounts already paid by the Authority under
-- Part 2A ... (b) the present value of the amounts that the Authority estimates will become payable ... in the future";
-- s 54(10) the Authority's certificate is evidence of it. s 54(2) "reduced in proportion to the participant's share in
-- the responsibility for the injury" where the participant was contributorily negligent. s 54(3) from another person at
-- fault, "such proportion ... as corresponds to the person's share in the responsibility for the injury" (fork F10: the
-- s 54(2) reduction is not applied again to that share). The owner and driver are liable "jointly or either of them
-- severally" (s 54(5)(a)): the amount is what may be recovered from either. Where the Authority cannot recover, 0.
-- A percentage outside 0 to 100: NOTHING.
@export How much can the Lifetime Care and Support Authority recover from me for an injured participant's treatment and care (s 54(2), (3), (4))?
GIVEN `my part in the accident` IS A `My part in the accident` @desc Your part in the accident. One of: "I owned the vehicle and was driving it", "I owned the vehicle and someone else was driving it", "I was driving the vehicle and someone else owned it", "I was partly at fault but was not the owner or driver of a motor vehicle", "none of these"
      `the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the participant's injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver of the vehicle in its use or operation
      `no third-party policy was in force for the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the accident, there was no NSW compulsory third-party policy in force for the vehicle
      `the vehicle was covered by an interstate or Commonwealth compulsory scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was covered by compulsory third-party personal injury insurance, or a compulsory motor accident compensation scheme, under the law of a place other than New South Wales or of the Commonwealth
      `Chapter 3 of the 1999 Act applies to the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is one to which Chapter 3 of the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999 applies (under section 3B of that Act)
      `the vehicle did not have to be registered or insured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was, at the time, not required to be registered, exempt from registration, or (if it had to be registered) not required to be insured under the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999
      `the participant bought in under section 7A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured participant paid the Authority a contribution to buy into the Scheme under section 7A for these injuries
      `the court is satisfied someone drove without my authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are the owner and someone else was driving: whether you establish to the court's satisfaction that the driver was driving without your authority
      `the court is satisfied of the driver's defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were the driver and someone else owned the vehicle: whether you establish to the court's satisfaction that you drove with the owner's authority (or reasonably believed so) and reasonably believed a third-party policy was in force
      `the amount the Authority has already paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the Authority has already paid for the participant's treatment and care needs from this injury, in dollars
      `the present value of what the Authority estimates it will pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The present value of the amounts the Authority estimates it will pay in future for those needs, in dollars (as in the Authority's certificate)
      `the participant's share of responsibility` IS A NUMBER @desc The participant's own share in the responsibility for the injury through contributory negligence, as a percentage (0 if none)
      `my share of responsibility` IS A NUMBER @desc If you were partly at fault but not the owner or driver of a motor vehicle: your share in the responsibility for the injury, as a percentage (any number otherwise)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much can the Authority recover from me` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the participant's share of responsibility` LESS THAN 0 OR `the participant's share of responsibility` GREATER THAN 100 THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (no such share)
           IF `my part in the accident` EQUALS `I was partly at fault but was not the owner or driver of a motor vehicle` AND (`my share of responsibility` LESS THAN 0 OR `my share of responsibility` GREATER THAN 100) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (no such share)
           IF `can recover` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST 0
           IF `my part in the accident` EQUALS `I was partly at fault but was not the owner or driver of a motor vehicle` THEN JUST ((`the present value` TIMES `my share of responsibility`) DIVIDED BY 100)
           OTHERWISE JUST ((`the present value` TIMES (100 MINUS `the participant's share of responsibility`)) DIVIDED BY 100)
    WHERE
        `the present value` MEANS `the amount the Authority has already paid` PLUS `the present value of what the Authority estimates it will pay`
        `can recover` MEANS `the Authority may recover under s 54 from` `my part in the accident` `fault` `the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver` `uninsured` `no third-party policy was in force for the vehicle` `interstate` `the vehicle was covered by an interstate or Commonwealth compulsory scheme` `chapter 3` `Chapter 3 of the 1999 Act applies to the injury` `exempt` `the vehicle did not have to be registered or insured` `bought in` `the participant bought in under section 7A` `owner's defence` `the court is satisfied someone drove without my authority` `driver's defence` `the court is satisfied of the driver's defence`
